    "7295708a2ed7572ba57032d9a112917638750f88053cd7b9427a46824327c8c1": {
      "normalizationVersion": 1,
      "sourceHash": "a63a7dbc3bbfc1af4aa10808503eea8da846356ec649475e3a08d643782347c2",
      "contextFingerprint": "70d4b9ac3769ce9f6b4b6b6fcb0f1d8943b4ebc1d9129549de31a91445066703",
      "sourceText": "| 需求 | 推荐写法 | 说明 |\n|:---|:---|:---|\n| `double` 转 `int` | `static_cast<int>(x)` | 明确可能丢失小数 |\n| `enum class` 转整数 | `static_cast<int>(e)` | 枚举类不会隐式转整数 |\n| 基类指针转派生类指针，并且不确定真实类型 | `dynamic_cast<Derived*>(p)` | 转换失败可判断 `nullptr` |\n| 去掉 `const` 适配旧接口 | `const_cast<T*>(p)` | 前提是旧接口不会修改真正的 const 对象 |\n| 指针和整数互转、底层字节解释 | `reinterpret_cast<T>(x)` | 非常底层，优先避免 |",
      "translatedText": "| Requirement | Recommended写法 | Description |\n|:---|:---|:---|\n| `double` cast to `int` | `static_cast<int>(x)` | Explicitly acknowledges possible loss of fractional part |\n| `enum class` cast to integer | `static_cast<int>(e)` | Enum classes are not implicitly converted to integers |\n| Base class pointer to derived class pointer, and the actual type is uncertain | `dynamic_cast<Derived*>(p)` | Conversion failure can be checked with `nullptr` |\n|  remove `const` adapt to legacy interface | `const_cast<T*>(p)` | Provided that the legacy interface does not modify the actual const object |\n| Pointer\\-to\\-integer conversion and low\\-level byte interpretation | `reinterpret_cast<T>(x)` | Very low\\-level; avoid if possible |",
